{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Jira 3.10.5 seam evidence (2026-08-17): in this dedicated worktree venv, inspect.signature(jira.JIRA.__init__) exposes top-level max_retries: int = 3; installed source assigns self._session.max_retries = max_retries. A credential-free/no-network construction probe using JIRA(server=\"https://jira.invalid\", token_auth=\"probe\", get_server_info=False, max_retries=0) completed and produced client._session.max_retries == 0. Implementation must preserve a real-client constructor test for that exact pinned-version path and fail loud if it changes. Follow-up on pycontribs/jira issue #789: the report was against jira 2.0.0, Python 3.7, and basic_auth during eager server_info authentication; it was stale-closed in 2019. Rebar's DC seam is pinned to jira 3.10.5, uses token_auth, and the constructor oracle disables server-info network I/O, so #789 does not contradict the verified constructor/read-back capability. S3 venue-gated validation remains the owner of real authentication/cutover evidence."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787033810576125001,"uuid":"04e7b65d-d086-4286-8f01-62aba7781a1e"}